# Layer-1 encoding patterns

> Module SaraPattern

> Using SaraWorld as W

This file is not part of the statute port. It pins down, in typechecked Catala,
the three encoding patterns every Layer-1 section will use, so that the shape of
the port is settled before 3,283 lines of Prolog get translated against it.

## Pattern 1 — case-injected conclusions

154 of the 376 SARA cases (41%) assert the *conclusion* of a statute predicate
rather than let it be derived: `s152_c_1(bob,alice,2015).` appears directly in
`s151_c_pos.pl`. 213 such injections span 30 predicates, and 255 of the injected
rows carry don't-care arguments (`s2_b(alice,_,2017)` — "qualifies, amount
irrelevant").

A Layer-1 scope therefore cannot simply compute its output. It takes the
injection as an optional input, and Catala's default logic supplies exactly the
right semantics: the derived definition is the base case, and the injection is
an exception that takes priority when present. This is the mechanism SARA
simulates by consulting a predicate that the case file has added clauses to.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope DependantQualifies:
  input world content W.World
  input dependant content W.Entity
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## Present when the case injects this conclusion instead of deriving it.
  input injected content optional of boolean
  output qualifies content boolean
```

```catala
scope DependantQualifies:
  ## The derived reading: some birth event links the two in the taxable year.
  ## (Placeholder body -- the real 152(c)(1) test lands in the section port.)
  definition qualifies equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      (ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Son
       or ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Daughter)
      and ev.agents contains dependant
      and ev.patients contains taxpayer

  ## The case's assertion wins where it is present.
  exception definition qualifies
    under condition injected with pattern Present
    consequence equals
      match injected with pattern
      -- Present content v: v
      -- Absent: false
```

## Pattern 2 — optional dates

`utils.pl` reads an unbound `End` as "the relationship is still ongoing", via
`\+ end_(Relationship,_)`. That distinction is load-bearing: a marriage with no
end date is current, not one that ended at some sentinel time. Layer 0 stores
role values as lists, so absence is the empty list and `List.first_element`
lifts it into an `optional`, keeping the `var`/`nonvar` reading explicit.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope RelationshipWindow:
  input ev content W.Event
  output starts_on content optional of date
  output ends_on content optional of date
  output is_ongoing content boolean
```

```catala
scope RelationshipWindow:
  definition starts_on equals List.first_element of ev.starts
  definition ends_on equals List.first_element of ev.ends
  definition is_ongoing equals ends_on with pattern Absent
```

## Pattern 3 — stratified cycle entry

§151 → §68 → §63 → §151 and §152 ⇄ §7703 are genuine cycles in the statutes.
Catala computes a dependency order over definitions and rejects circular ones
outright, so the port breaks each cycle at a documented point: the cycle-entry
conclusion becomes an explicit input, and the harness supplies the preliminary
value. The stratification is fixed here in Layer 0 rather than left to Layer 1,
so that every future sample sees the same one and stays comparable.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope MaritalStatusStratified:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## §7703 consults §152, and §152 consults §7703. This input carries the
  ## preliminary §152 verdict, computed first with the §7703 dependency
  ## defaulted. See sara_scripts/DEVIATIONS.md.
  input dependant_prelim content boolean
  output is_married content boolean
```

```catala
scope MaritalStatusStratified:
  definition is_married equals
    (exists ev among world.events such that
       ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Marriage
       and ev.agents contains taxpayer)
    and not dependant_prelim
```
